caption: Technique Made Flesh
tradition-component: technique-made-flesh

After mastering a Shadow Arts Jutsu tree, each Jutsu in that mastered tree whose primary effect is a finite-duration self-buff grants permission to purchase the permanent version of that self-buff as an ordinary advantage or advantage package, provided the practitioner's Shadow Arts Potence is at least three levels higher than the minimum Potence required to learn that Jutsu.

The permanent traits cost their normal GURPS character-point value and may receive normal applicable Shido discounts. This is purchase permission only; it grants no free character points and waives no general trait cap, prerequisite, or legality rule. Once purchased permanently, the traits are no longer being activated as that Jutsu: they do not inherit the Jutsu's finite duration, FP activation cost, or Jutsu Anchor roll unless the underlying permanent trait itself has such a rule. If the Jutsu contains multiple constituents, only the self-buff traits that make up its primary self-buff package gain this permanent-purchase permission; external attacks, Afflictions, environmental effects, or other non-self-buff constituents do not become permanent through this rule.
